<title>UK: BALTIC FREIGHT INDEX ROSE TWO POINTS TO 1,283.</title>
<headline>BALTIC FREIGHT INDEX ROSE TWO POINTS TO 1,283.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for</p>
<p>spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,283 today from</p>
<p>1,281 on Aug 12, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals</p>
<p>1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates</p>
<p>in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1353    12.281	  1353    12.288</p>
<p>   1a   1257  9519.000	  1256  9513.000</p>
<p>   2    1572    22.463	  1570    22.431</p>
<p>   2a   1498 12281.000	  1498 12288.000</p>
<p>   3    1384    12.769	  1386    12.788</p>
<p>   3a   1169  9225.000	  1165  9194.000</p>
<p>   6    1288    13.288	  1285    13.250</p>
<p>   7    1178     5.738	  1175     5.719</p>
<p>   8     843     9.269	   843     9.269</p>
<p>   9     704  6156.000	   699  6113.000</p>
<p>  10    1144     5.781	  1141     5.763</p>
